    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** standing as our clear analytical anchor, boasting an elite score of 82.13. His leadoff positioning against the vulnerable Junk (xERA 4.67) creates a massive opportunity for run production, further bolstered by a 14% dynamic platoon advantage. While **Yordan Alvarez** remains a cornerstone of our lineup, his matchup against Logan Gilbert\u2014a high-end arm (xERA 3.42)\u2014tempered his efficiency score to 60.70; however, his elite 0.442 xwOBA justifies his presence regardless of the tougher SP environment. We are also looking for a strong performance from **Junior Caminero**, who maintains a score of 61.55 despite facing a quality southpaw in Fried, thanks primarily to his high-leverage #3 spot in the order.\n\nTactical adjustments remain critical as we monitor the scarcity of stolen bases. **Trea Turner** offers a stable floor of 64.77, though his upside is slightly capped by the matchup against May. Conversely, **Hector Rodriguez** provides sneaky value (60.91) as a result of the favorable 4.89 xERA of Ritchie, and we are relying on **Chase Meidroth** (58.69) to provide steady contributions at SS as he benefits from a positive dynamic platoon adjustment against Lynch IV. Unfortunately, our bench options have been decimated by external factors; **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** were both prime candidates for deployment, but their respective postponements forced them to the bench entirely, while **Colt Keith** and **Lars Nootbaar** remain unavailable due to injury and lineup exclusion.\n\nThe primary risk profile for today centers on our lower-tier starters like **Jacob Gonzalez**, who sits at a marginal 43.53 score due to a bottom-of-the-order assignment, and **Carson Benge**, who faces a significant 9% downgrade due to the L/L platoon disadvantage against Gore. We will monitor the status of **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Casey Sc